      "point_1_the_formal_semantics_of_can_know": "In standard epistemic logic and benchmark design, what does 'Yvette can know' mean? Under Model 4, Yvette deduces $T_C = 0$ solely from Christopher's public announcement of ignorance. But why did Christopher announce ignorance? If $A$ or $B$ were thirsty ($T_A=1$ or $T_B=1$), could Christopher have known whether someone is thirsty? No. BUT under standard DEL public announcement protocol, an agent announces ignorance only if their epistemic state permits it. If the protocol requires polling or common knowledge of the announcement conditions, Model 4 creates an ungrounded event.",
