      "point_3_the_ai_benchmark_ground_truth_precedent": "Appeal directly to benchmark curation literature (e.g., BIG-bench Epistemic Reasoning, LogiQA, SCONE): benchmark tasks that specify '$N$ agents', 'all visible to each other', and 'worlds model boolean properties' are 100% deterministically generated from the Muddy Children / Hat frame. Automated benchmark answer keys do not compute folk-psychological interoception; they execute the Kripke update $[!\\bigwedge \\neg K_i (\\bigvee T_x)] W$, which mathematically outputs $|\\{(0,0,0,0)\\}| = 1$."
